From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:34:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7001-air2: Add Lightning charging

iBoot leaves the D2207's input-current limit at 100 mA, so the iPad Air 2
drains on a cable. Describe the Tristar (CBTL1610) at i2c0 0x1a and the
Lightning charger on the PMIC, with the PMU line (112) and ADC done (89).
The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input. Link the charger
to the USB device controller, which reports the host's allowance to it.

No source events. With the plug event (0) subscribed, it stays unmasked
when the iPad is reset into DFU from a running Linux; that reset skips
iBoot, which would mask it. The cable replugs of the next boot latch it,
and that boot froze before userspace, then the watchdog reset it: 4 to 5
times out of 5 after a charging session. Without it, 3 of 3 such resets
booted. The charger's 100 ms poll of the connection state sees plug and
unplug instead.

On a J81 the charger identifies a Mac's USB-C port as a BC1.2 charging
port and an Apple USB-C power adapter by its 1.5 A advertisement, and
grants 1500 mA for both; the battery goes from about -0.7 A to +0.9 A.
Unplugging withdraws the grant, and the next plug identifies the source
again.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
index 246790a7f..d6092dcc3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
@@ -130,6 +130,12 @@ &serial0 {
 &i2c0 {
 	status = "okay";
 
+	/* The Lightning port controller, from the ADT i2c0/tristar node. */
+	tristar: port-controller@1a {
+		compatible = "nxp,cbtl1610";
+		reg = <0x1a>;
+	};
+
 	pmic@3c {
 		compatible = "apple,arabela-pmic", "apple,i2c-pmic";
 		reg = <0x3c>;
@@ -155,6 +161,37 @@ pmu_gpio: gpio {
 			apple,wake-events = <0x24>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Lightning charging, at the D2207's registers as iOS 15.8
+		 * AppleD2207PMU uses them: connection and charger state at
+		 * 0x60, the input-current limit at 0x4c0, the ADC at 0x500.
+		 * The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input.
+		 */
+		tristar_charger: charger@60 {
+			compatible = "apple,j81-tristar-charger", "apple,d2207-tristar-charger";
+			reg = <0x60 0x0d>, <0x4c0 0x01>, <0x500 0x04>;
+			reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
+			interrupt-parent = <&pmu_gpio>;
+			/*
+			 * The PMU line and ADC done. No source events: the plug
+			 * event (0) stays unmasked across a reset that bypasses
+			 * iBoot (DFU entered from Linux), latches on the replugs
+			 * of the next boot and froze that boot. The charger's
+			 * 100 ms poll of 0x60 sees plug and unplug.
+			 */
+			interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+				     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+			apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
+			input-current-limit-microamp = <2400000>;
+
+			/* The charger decides when USB data may come on. */
+			port {
+				tristar_charger_usb: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&usbdev_role>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
 		rtc@5c0 {
 			compatible = "apple,arabela-pmic-rtc", "apple,amber-pmic-rtc";
 			reg = <0x5c0 0x10>;
@@ -259,6 +296,18 @@ &touchclk {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* Tell the Lightning charger what the USB host allows. */
+&usbdev {
+	usb-psy-name = "lightning";
+	usb-role-switch;
+
+	port {
+		usbdev_role: endpoint {
+			remote-endpoint = <&tristar_charger_usb>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 /*
  * The BCM4350C2's Bluetooth on UART3, from the ADT uart3/bluetooth node:
  * power enable on D2207 GPIO 2, BT_WAKE on GPIO 164. m1n1 adds the device
